    "bio": "A Representative from Illinois; born in Rockford, Winnebago County, Ill., March 24, 1944; graduated from Auburn High School, Rockford, Ill., 1962; B.A., American University, Washington, D.C., 1967; J.D., Marquette University School of Law, Milwaukee, Wis., 1970; lawyer, private practice; unsuccessful candidate for nomination to the One Hundred Second Congress in 1990; member, Republican National Committee; elected as a Republican to the One Hundred Third and to the nine succeeding Congresses (January 3, 1993-January 3, 2013); chair, Committee on Small Business (One Hundred Seventh through One Hundred Ninth Congresses); unsuccessful candidate for nomination to the One Hundred Thirteenth Congress in 2012.",
